  ,"providerPrivacyPolicyContent": "PRIVACY POLICY FOR PROVIDERS\n\nMultiBook processes provider account and business data to publish and manage stays or services. This includes your business profile, location, photos, prices, availability, staff, promotions, bookings, appointments, earnings and customer messages.\n\n1. Customer data\nFor confirmed reservations you receive only the data needed to deliver the stay or service: name, contact details, selected dates/time, offering and relevant booking details. Use it only for that reservation. Do not sell it, share it without a legal basis or use it for unsolicited marketing.\n\n2. Security and records\nKeep provider access secure and limit staff access to authorized people. Never request passwords, CVV codes or full card details in chat. Messages, reviews, cancellations, no-show records and transaction snapshots may be retained for support, fraud prevention, disputes, financial reporting and legal obligations.\n\n3. Your choices\nYou can update business data in Manage Stays & Services. For account deletion, data access or privacy questions, contact MultiBook support. Material policy changes will be communicated in the app."
  ,"providerTermsOfServiceContent": "TERMS OF SERVICE FOR PROVIDERS\n\nBy operating a business on MultiBook, you agree to these provider terms. MultiBook gives independent businesses tools to publish stays or services, manage availability and communicate with customers.\n\n1. Accurate listings\nKeep business information, prices, availability, amenities, staff and service descriptions accurate. Do not publish misleading photos, offers or availability.\n\n2. Reservations and payments\nA confirmed booking or appointment is an agreement between your business and the customer. Honor it unless a valid exceptional reason applies. Use decline, cancellation, rescheduling and cash no-show controls accurately. Online and cash payments are recorded separately; you remain responsible for taxes, invoices, refunds and applicable legal obligations.\n\n3. Conduct and enforcement\nUse customer data only to provide the reserved stay or service. Professional communication is required; discrimination, harassment, spam, review manipulation and payment requests outside approved flows are prohibited. We may restrict listings or accounts that endanger users or misuse the platform.\n\n4. Changes\nWe may update these terms for legal, security or product reasons. Continued use after publication means acceptance of the updated terms."
